    {
      "title": "Iran unveils ‘We will kill Trump’ banner – but US president may now be tempted to resume bombing",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/joy-iran-trump-defeat-us-midterm-elections-war",
      "description": "<p>Iran celebrates its claimed role in ‘regime change’ amid pressure on Trump to ‘finish the job’ with attack</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/nov/04/dollar-falls-while-gold-us-treasury-bonds-rally-markets-react-democrats-midterm-election-victory-marks-spencer-latest-live-updates\">US midterms live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Iran this week unveiled a huge billboard and banners over Enqelab Square in central Tehran. The billboard pledged in English: “We will kill Trump” – elevating the degree of personal animus with which Donald Trump is viewed in official Iranian circles.</p><p>The poster depicts the US president behind bars with his head bowed. And in a sense, given <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">the US midterm election results</a> on Tuesday, Iran has indeed killed Trump, or at least the second term of his presidency. Trump’s reverse is all the more piquant because it comes on the day Iran’s leadership celebrates the anniversary of the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/nov/05/iranian-students-take-over-us-embassy-tehran-iran-1979\">seizure of the US embassy in Tehran</a> in 1979, an event that ensnared Jimmy Carter, and a reminder of how Iran has ruined the prospects of more than one US president.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/joy-iran-trump-defeat-us-midterm-elections-war\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T14:07:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "US midterm elections 2026 live updates: Trump defiant about brutal Republican losses and acknowledges Iran war’s unpopularity",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/04/midterm-elections-results-senate-house-michigan-maine-mississippi-latest-updates",
      "description": "<p>President again insisted that if he were on the ballot Republicans would have won, despite historic losses: ‘They just couldn’t transfer that love’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">Full report: Democrats win control of Congress</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/tell-us-how-do-you-feel-about-the-us-midterm-election-results\">Tell us: how do you feel about the midterm results?</a></p></li></ul><p>Wall Street surged at the open, after Democrats scored historic victories in midterm elections and secured control of US Congress.</p><p>The Dow Jones rose 2%, while the tech-heavy Nasdaq and the benchmark S&amp;P 500 both gained more than 1%. That’s quite a reversal: Overnight, stock futures fell sharply as investors worried about the prospect of tougher regulation of the AI sector and the impact on economic growth.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/04/midterm-elections-results-senate-house-michigan-maine-mississippi-latest-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T18:51:45"
    },
    {
      "title": "US voters rebuke Trump as Democrats win control of Congress in ‘blue wave’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results",
      "description": "<p>President’s party stripped of control after he spent weeks pleading with Americans to pretend he was on ballot</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/04/midterm-elections-results-senate-house-michigan-maine-mississippi-latest-updates\">US midterm elections – live updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/04/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/midterm-election-results-question-answer\">Tell us: what do you want to know about the midterm election results?</a></p></li></ul><p>Donald Trump has been dealt a devastating blow to his authority with a succession of crushing defeats in the midterm elections, in which his Republican party was stripped of control of the Senate and the House as his handpicked “Maga” candidates were swept away by a blue tsunami.</p><p>The president spent weeks before the election pleading with the American people to pretend he was on the ballot. He may now rue that tactic: the American people took him at his word, and delivered him a bloody nose of historic proportions, flinging his presidency into lame duck status.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T17:15:38"
    },
    {
      "title": "JD Vance says US war on Iran is ‘real reason’ Republicans lost midterm elections",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/jd-vance-iran-war-midterms-election",
      "description": "<p>Stance signals vice-president seeks to distance himself from the unpopular conflict ahead of possible 2028 run</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/04/midterm-elections-results-senate-house-michigan-maine-mississippi-latest-updates\">US midterms 2026 live – latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/midterm-election-results-question-answer\">Tell us: what do you want to know about the results?</a></p></li></ul><p>JD Vance said on Wednesday that the war against Iran doomed the Republican party in the US midterm elections, which are widely seen as a sweeping rebuke of Donald Trump’s presidency.</p><p>The intervention signals that the vice-president, once the face of the Trump administration’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jun/25/jd-vance-iran-peace-deal\">deal-making efforts</a> with Tehran, seeks to distance himself from the unpopular conflict before a possible 2028 White House run.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/jd-vance-iran-war-midterms-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T17:15:33"
    },
